## Format

The original demonstration format is `STKDEMO1` (eight ASCII bytes), a little-endian signed
32-bit record count (0–64), then that many signed 32-bit values. Files are limited to 1 MiB.
There is no crypto, compression or checksum in this synthetic format. Trailing bytes are
uninterpreted and preserved. `example.bin` is the synthetic fixture's only file role.
Record offsets are stable only because there are no structural writes.

